# Encoding test fixtures must round-trip byte-for-byte.
#
# These files hold deliberate byte sequences that the test suite asserts on:
# exact UTF-8/Big5 boundary offsets, a fixture with no trailing newline, and a
# fixture whose CRLF line endings are the thing under test. Git's line-ending
# normalization (core.autocrlf) would rewrite those bytes on checkout, shifting
# every offset and breaking the suite on any machine that clones fresh.
#
# -text disables all normalization so the bytes are stored and restored verbatim.
test/fixtures/*.txt -text
